WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.176
(thunder crashes)

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:12.054
- Jake, he accused you of murder
in a public forum.

00:00:12.137 --> 00:00:13.680
- No one takes that seriously.

00:00:13.764 --> 00:00:15.641
That's what kids do.
They just try to sound cool.

00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:18.185
That's all it is. Honest.

00:00:21.897 --> 00:00:25.943
- The book grew out of my
experiences as a prosecutor.

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:28.987
Mark preserved
the essence of the novel,

00:00:29.071 --> 00:00:32.074
which is this isn't
a crime story about a family,

00:00:32.157 --> 00:00:33.408
this is a family story

00:00:33.492 --> 00:00:34.743
that happens to be
about a crime.

00:00:34.826 --> 00:00:36.411
- They really think I killed Ben.

00:00:36.495 --> 00:00:39.331
- It's a mistake.
We're gonna figure it out. Don't worry.

00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:43.043
- For me, the fun
of being a screenwriter

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:44.545
is finding source
material and saying

00:00:44.628 --> 00:00:48.215
what's the best cinematic
version of this story.

00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:51.552
- What was so exciting was that
you could open the story up

00:00:51.635 --> 00:00:57.266
to explore all of these possibilities
that series TV allows you to do.

00:00:58.559 --> 00:01:00.894
- The first time Mark gave me
all the episodes,

00:01:00.978 --> 00:01:02.688
I was like, all right,
I'll just read one tonight.

00:01:02.771 --> 00:01:04.273
And, you know,
you get to the end

00:01:04.356 --> 00:01:06.358
and you're, like, aah, I gotta
read the next one now.

00:01:07.651 --> 00:01:10.362
- We have Morten Tyldum
directing all eight episodes,

00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:12.865
so it really has a uniformity
of directorial vision.

00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:15.200
- I loved working with Mark on this.

00:01:15.284 --> 00:01:17.536
It was great to work very
closely together.

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:19.746
We knew exactly what
we liked, what we wanted to do.

00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:25.919
- To see Morten work,
and realize how high the standards are,

00:01:26.003 --> 00:01:29.798
explains how he's able to
achieve what he achieved on screen.

00:01:31.008 --> 00:01:33.468
- 14, they already got him on murder.

00:01:33.552 --> 00:01:35.304
You get to choose.

00:01:35.387 --> 00:01:39.433
You can be a good man,
or you can be a good father.

00:01:40.309 --> 00:01:42.436
- One of the challenges
in adapting it is that

00:01:42.519 --> 00:01:44.646
I don't want it to be limited to
just Andy's perspective.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.941
I want it to be Laurie's perspective,
Jacob's perspective.

00:01:49.026 --> 00:01:50.569
- In doing adaptations,
you're not seeing it

00:01:50.652 --> 00:01:52.821
through the eyes of the cops,
or the victim's.

00:01:52.905 --> 00:01:55.199
You're actually seeing it
through this family.

00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:58.994
- To have these incredibly
exciting actors,

00:01:59.077 --> 00:02:01.413
who differ from
the characters in the book

00:02:01.496 --> 00:02:05.292
with respect to their age
or their appearance, is wonderful.

00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:06.668
- He didn't do this.
I know he didn't.

00:02:06.752 --> 00:02:08.003
- No, you don't.

00:02:08.086 --> 00:02:09.296
- No one can sustain that level
of deception.

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:10.797
- Of course, he could.

00:02:11.256 --> 00:02:13.342
- Bill's book, and the show
even more so,

00:02:13.425 --> 00:02:18.388
really tries to explore how dark
can you believe Jacob is,

00:02:18.472 --> 00:02:21.058
and still hold on to
this glimmer of hope

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:22.684
that it's impossible
he could've done this.

00:02:23.352 --> 00:02:25.687
- I didn't do it.
I swear.

00:02:25.771 --> 00:02:27.314
- Do you know what's at stake?

00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:29.441
Do you realize
what they want to do to you?

00:02:29.525 --> 00:02:31.109
- Stop, you're scaring him!

00:02:31.193 --> 00:02:33.737
- Good! He should be scared!

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.030
I'm scared!

